# Test: lambda closure capturing an enclosing function's parameter.
# Before the fix, the lambda captured variable names dynamically: when
# the enclosing function returned, its parameter scope was popped, so
# the captured variable resolved to null at call time (printing "null").
# After the fix, the lambda snapshots the visible lexical environment
# at creation time and restores it when called.
fn, adder(n)
    return, fn(x) x + n
/end
set, add5, adder(5)
set, add10, adder(10)
println, add5(3)
println, add10(3)
# Expected output: 8 / 13
